# Preserve existing store content

When the user asks to improve, redesign, polish, or deploy the site:

## Do not remove unless explicitly asked
- Do not delete UI sections, nav links, pages, features, or copy the user did not ask to remove.
- Do not clear, null out, or overwrite `imageUrl` / product images / category images / banners in code or seed.
- Do not reset catalog, orders, stock, or settings as part of a “fix”.
- Prefer additive changes: improve styles/layout around existing content.

## Production data safety (Railway)
- Uploads live under `/app/uploads` (must stay on a Volume).
- SQLite lives under `/data` (recommend a Volume at `/data`).
- Never change upload paths, volume mount assumptions, or `DATABASE_URL` in a way that orphans existing files.
- Do not enable destructive seed/purge on production (`ALLOW_SEED`, purge-demo) unless the user explicitly requests it.
- On deploy-related work, warn if a change could wipe ephemeral disk or DB without volumes.

## Before shipping an improvement
- Confirm the change does not drop existing images, categories, products, or checkout/cart behavior.
- If a redesign would hide or remove something, ask first — do not assume.
